module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.emitter_change_lands_without_regenerating_its_generated_workflow

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data emitter_change_lands_without_regenerating_its_generated_workflow: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "emitter_change_lands_without_regenerating_its_generated_workflow" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a PR changes the bash emitter (or any DAG authority whose output feeds a generated workflow), its own witness controls pass, heal passes because the generated workflow is not in the PR's diff or in the regen-affected-scope, and the commit lands. The committed generated artifact is now STALE: it reflects the old emitter, not the new one. The next PR that regenerates from the merged tree sees the delta, which can include refusal markers where the old emitter produced working shell.",

    "RECEIPT, gunbc#16190 (2026-11-12). PR #16270 (session/nimble-crab-475, b31255100485, 2026-11-12T01:03:16Z) rewrote the bash emitter: added name validation to bash_build_word_var (refuses names that are not valid bash identifiers), changed and_or pair parenthesization, introduced double-quoted command substitution, and migrated the sol_hold DAG to use BracketQuoted spelling. The commit did NOT regenerate .github/workflows/fleet-converge.yml. heal passed because the workflow file was not in the PR's diff. When #16190 next regenerated from the merged tree, three REFUSED markers appeared: SOL_RELEASE, SOL_OWNED, and the boot trap body. The markers came from the new builder refusing shv(name: \"1\") (positional parameter, not a valid identifier) and bash_build_word_var(name: \"?\") (exit-status parameter) — constructs the old emitter rendered as var expansions.",

    "WHY HEAL MISSES IT: heal's regen-affected-scope regenerates artifacts in the claim set whose SOURCE FILES changed in the PR. The fleet-converge workflow is generated by dag/gunbc/instruments/generated_artifact_gate.dag, but its inputs include the ENTIRE DAG tree (every step in the workflow comes from some DAG module). A change to the bash emitter's internals (src/v2/extdeps/languages/bash_build.dag, src/v2/workflow/bash_command_fold_serialize.dag) is not the DIRECT authority of the generated file in the regen-scoping sense, so the regen does not re-generate fleet-converge.yml for that PR.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: after any change to the emitter, builder, or any DAG module that feeds a generated workflow's content (not just the workflow's own DAG), regenerate the affected generated artifact and verify it against the committed copy. A passing witness suite does not prove the generated artifact is current.",

    "FIX APPLIED (this PR): sol_hold.dag replaced shv(name: \"1\") with the proper bash_build_word_positional constructor and shv(name: \"?\") with bash_build_word_exit_status(). mtcollins1_boot_step.dag replaced all bash_build_word_var(name: \"?\") with bash_build_word_exit_status(). Two new witness controls in bash_command_fold.dag test the positional-assign and exit-status-assign paths that regressed.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.sol_hold", decl_name: "sol_hold_record_read"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.mtcollins1_boot_step", decl_name: "gunbc_ci_mtcollins1_boot_trap_body"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.bash_build", decl_name: "bash_build_word_var"),
  ],
}
